1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,560
An agent has one read left. Which source should it open, and what happens if the evidence behind that choice changes?

2
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:17,280
This archived question asks for a paternal grandfather. Matching words in the first passage selects a page for the surname.

3
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:25,680
We reveal the reference titles after the choice. The first read and the literal match cover one of the two required pages.

4
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:34,800
Change only the passage evidence to verified hyperlinks. The stored anchor now leads to the page for Gabriel-Elzéar Taschereau.

5
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:42,480
Reveal the reference again. Both supporting pages are now covered, with the same budget of two reads.

6
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:52,080
Suppress just that link. A different person takes the second slot. The audit shows that only one supporting page remains.

7
00:00:52,080 --> 00:01:00,720
Now open an archived coding session from pytest. The three files on the right are the agent’s original final context.

8
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:10,200
With four static rankings, the next read opens the deprecations document. The receipt gives a pinned line range and content digest.

9
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:17,440
The evaluator opens a separate annotation database. This read adds no required file.

10
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:25,680
Replace the fourth ranking with the agent’s suggestions. The same one-read budget now opens the acceptance tests.

11
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:39,160
The evaluator confirms a hit here. Across 283 sessions, the suggestion-first rule yielded 20 new hits, compared with 26 for the four-billion-parameter embedding model.

12
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:49,400
In this tool trace, each producer scores one point per unit of outgoing support. Two SQLite queries reconstruct revision sixteen.

13
00:01:49,400 --> 00:02:00,200
Advance to revision seventeen. Producer fourteen loses an edge to nineteen. Its score falls to one, and producer three wins the tie.

14
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:09,480
Read revision sixteen again. Both queries restore producer fourteen, even though the committed history still includes the withdrawal.

15
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:18,520
The interval query rebuilds support from historical edges. The journal reads its last winner entry at or before the requested version.

16
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:28,720
This replay uses two real tox commits. Before the change, thirty distinct Python files import the parser, which ranks eighth.

17
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:38,960
Advance the commit. Its score falls to twenty-nine. The cached bound certifies that no omitted file can overtake it under the tie rule.

18
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:49,400
The recorded SQLite counters show one row fetched by the variable-prefix baseline and zero by the bound. Both return the exact same eight files.

19
00:02:49,400 --> 00:03:01,800
Increase the cache to twelve. Both methods avoid the lookup. Only one of 714 Git transitions across six projects separated the two at capacity eight.

20
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:13,160
Each view lets a visitor change the evidence, repeat a read, and inspect the result. The local artifact includes the database projections and replay scripts.
